samples (ubuntu-latest)	run every sample	2026-10-23T14:09:55.5088774Z samples: PENDING ch05/ex5-8 [run(exit=0, stdout="marmot 5")] — blocker: TWO blockers, re-measured at bs50 against wolf 0.2.15 / lupin 0.1.37, and NEITHER is the one this row used to name. (1) `sorted_by` exists now — it is one of `[type.comb.set]`'s ten — but it is a `std.list` function that must reach its home module, and this repository configures no std root for either tool, so both machines decline at `[type.method.root]`: lupin `unsupported`, wolf E0301. That half is wolf-book#39, not a std-surface debt. (2) `.take(1)` can never arrive: `take` is a keyword, so `fn take` is E0008 on both machines and no std function may carry the name. This row is waiting on a spelling that cannot exist and the exercise wants rewriting (wolf-book#58). Re-measured at bs53 against wolf 0.2.17 / lupin 0.1.40, and identically against 0.2.16 / 0.1.38: lupin `unsupported` (`List.sorted_by` reaches `std.list` and no std root is configured), exit 4; wolf no longer says E0301 — it answers `cannot compile this yet — member access on a value whose type is still being inferred` at `resolve`, exit 4. wolf-book#39 closed on 2026-09-12 with the std posture recorded in `wolf-toolchain.toml`; its open successor is wolf-book#45. Re-measured at bs54 against wolf 0.2.18 / lupin 0.1.41, and identically against 0.2.17 / 0.1.40 the same hour: both answers unchanged, word for word, at the same span (@300..303). Re-measured at bs55 against wolf 0.2.19 / lupin 0.1.42 and 0.2.18 / 0.1.41 the same hour: identical on both pairs, word for word, same span. Re-measured at bs58 against wolf 0.2.21 / lupin 0.1.44 and 0.2.19 / 0.1.42 the same hour (release archives by digest, docs/audit/bs58-evidence/probes-control.txt and probes-subject.txt): identical on both pairs, word for word, same span. Re-measured at bs65 against wolf 0.2.28 / lupin 0.1.51 and 0.2.26 / 0.1.49 (release archives by digest on kasumi, hasu and nomad-1, docs/audit/bs65-evidence/*/probes.txt), and the two answers now depend on what sits beside `wolf`. With no `std/` beside it (0.2.26's archive; a bare `cargo build`) the compiler's answer is unchanged, `member access on a value whose type is still being inferred` at resolve, @300..303. From 0.2.28's archive whole, whose `std/` is the default std root (s204, ruling #59), `sorted_by` resolves and the compiler reaches the type checker with two errors: E0401 at the comparator (`fn(a, b) b.1 <=> a.1` answers `int` where `sorted_by`'s comparator must answer `bool`, a THIRD blocker, the exercise's own) and E0403 at `.take(1)` («`take` is the ownership verb, never a method», naming `xs[..n]`, which is #58's half). The book prints the archive whole and CI stages its `std/` (the bs65 ruling), so the compiler's answer of record is the second. lupin 0.1.51 still has no std root (its own archive carries none) and answers `unsupported` in s204's longer words, exit 4; exercise 5-8's console block is spliced from that run. (owner: wolf-book#45 (the std root; successor of the closed #39) + wolf-book#58 (the unspellable `take`))
